pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* The version 2.0 manifestation of defect 14 (order auxiliary variables are not
* order-private), ported from the ay repo's patch 0002-ay-post-fork-soundness-fixes.
* There it was filed under `incorrect/` because 0002 closed the hole by refusing
* the top-level aux-var assertion at ACCEPTANCE. This fork closes the same hole
* at the SCOPE-INJECTION point instead (`ScopeAuxVarNotFresh`, exercised by the
* version-3 companions `incorrect/version3/order_aux_var_asserted_top_level*`),
* and that check is enough because version 2.0 has NO `scope` construct at all:
* there is no way to inject the order's specification into a subproof, so the
* asserted `a1` can never be turned into a contradiction. This proof therefore
* verifies at exit 0 with `s VERIFIED NO CONCLUSION` and forges nothing — it is
* correct. Pinned here so a future change that DID make the v2 aux-var route
* forge a verdict would flip this to an accepting `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE` and
* fail the suite. See `ci/veripb-soundness/15-order-aux-var-not-private/`.
f 1
pre_order triv
    vars
        left u1
        right v1
        aux a1
    end
    spec
        red 1 ~a1 >= 1 ; a1 → 0 ; begin
        end
    end
    def
        -1 u1 1 v1 >= 0 ;
    end
    transitivity
        vars
            fresh_right w1
            fresh_aux_1 b1
            fresh_aux_2 c1
        end
        proof
            proofgoal #1
                p -2 -3 + -1 +
            end -1
        end
    end
end
load_order triv x1
red 1 a1 >= 1 ; a1 → 1 ; begin
end
output NONE
conclusion NONE
end pseudo-Boolean proof
